	<key>gen-thumb-info</key>
	<string> - "Prefer using embedded thumbnails" refers to prioritizing the use of thumbnails embedded within the image's EXIF data, which typically have lower resolution. However, since only the file header content needs to be read, it can significantly improve the speed of reading images on a network drive. As most images on the internet have their EXIF data removed to reduce file size, the program will then switch to "generate standard thumbnails."

 - "Generate standard thumbnails" refers to creating medium-quality thumbnails with a size of 512×512. In this case, the entire file content needs to be downloaded. (Since embedded thumbnails in RAW images usually have a higher resolution, their embedded thumbnails are still preferred in this mode.)

 - "Generate high-definition thumbnails" involves rendering the image precisely in the thumbnail area, and it is recommended to enable this option when the thumbnail size is larger than the default value. At this point, the re-rendered image may consume more memory.

Additionally, thumbnails are not generated for folders on external drives by default. Please go to "Settings" -&gt; "Advanced" to modify relevant options.</string>
