	<key>search-help</key>
	<string>**Filter Content**
The “Apply Filter” button filters the contents of the current directory, displaying only items that match the search criteria. To restore the original view, clear the search criteria and click this button again, or click the search icon in the toolbar.

**Search Subfolders**
To search files in subdirectories, first enable “Recursive Browse Mode”.

**What Are Regular Expressions?**
Regular expressions (regex) are patterns used to match character combinations within strings. They are a powerful text-processing tool widely used for tasks such as searching, replacing, and parsing text.
For example:
^2024 can match files starting with '2024';
.*modified\.[^.]+$ can match files ending with 'modified' (regardless of the extension);
.*\.jpg$ can match files with the '.jpg' extension.

**Advanced Search**
In “Recursive Browse Mode,” you can additionally use the “Use Full Path” option and combine it with regular expressions to perform advanced searches.
For example, given a full file path like:
/Users/Alice/Pictures/20220101/mypick/001.jpg
you can use the regular expression:
^.*\/[^\/]*pick[^\/]*\/[^\/]+$
to match all files whose parent directory names contain “pick.” For more complex regex patterns, you can use large language models to assist in writing them.</string>
