	<key>video-play-info</key>
	<string>In the player interface, pressing the left mouse button pauses playback, and right-click dragging adjusts the video playback progress. The keyboard left and right arrow keys can fast forward and rewind, and holding the Cmd key allows for frame-by-frame navigation.

macOS natively supports video formats such as "mp4", "mov", "m2ts", "ts", "mpeg", "mpg", "m4v", and "vob". Other formats still require an external player for playback.

For HEVC-encoded videos, macOS’s built-in decoder only recognizes codec tags of hvc1 and does not recognize tags of hev1. You can use FFmpeg to perform a lossless conversion: ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -c copy -movflags +faststart -tag:v hvc1 output.mp4.

Press Cmd+Shift+V to "Auto Play Visible Videos," meaning in thumbnail view, it will loop videos within the visible area. Pressing the shortcut again or switching folders will exit this mode.</string>
